<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Software on A Moment's Rest</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/tags/software/</link><description>Recent content in Software on A Moment's Rest</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:53:16 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.a-moment.top/en/tags/software/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>VS Code Might Actually Be an IDE</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/tools_note/vsc_remote/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Sep 2025 14:35:38 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/tools_note/vsc_remote/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://blog.a-moment.top/images/%E7%8C%9B%E7%8B%AC%E3%81%8C%E8%A5%B2%E3%81%86.png" alt="Featured image of post VS Code Might Actually Be an IDE" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Although VS Code&lt;sup id="fnref:1"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; is technically an editor, it actually feels more like an IDE (Integrated Development Environment) in disguise. And its most powerful feature is arguably its remote capabilities. Today, let&amp;rsquo;s talk about how to configure VS Code into a multi-purpose IDE that rivals Visual Studio&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The song I&amp;rsquo;ve chosen this time is a highly acclaimed Vocaloid track with countless covers, and one that I&amp;rsquo;m personally very fond of: &lt;strong&gt;猛独が襲う&lt;/strong&gt; (Moudoku ga Osou), written and composed by producer &lt;a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/hihumi_v" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;一二三 (Hifumi)&lt;/a&gt;. I happened to hear it at noon and thought it was fantastic, so I went with it. The featured image is from the equally stunning MV for this song, illustrated by &lt;a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/kyu_fu" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;休符 (Kyufu)&lt;/a&gt; — it&amp;rsquo;s really gorgeous~ I also have to point out that the incredible guitar work on this song was performed by &lt;a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/junjun_mimi03" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;じゅみ (Jumi)&lt;/a&gt;. I must immediately confess that the guitar is my favorite part of this song lol&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Setting Up an FRP Service</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/tools_note/frp_depoly/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 13:26:16 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/tools_note/frp_depoly/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://blog.a-moment.top/images/BagPipe.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Setting Up an FRP Service" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why do I have to first ToDesk into a Windows machine, and then SSH from that machine into the server just to connect!? Unbearable. Let&amp;rsquo;s just set up an FRP service myself.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The image features the lovely Ms. Bagpipe. According to unverified sources, it&amp;rsquo;s likely drawn by artist &lt;a class="link" href="https://weibo.com/u/5979033109" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;Liyu黎&lt;/a&gt; as a celebratory illustration for the 2022 Ambience Synesthesia concert. To match, let&amp;rsquo;s play Ms. Bagpipe&amp;rsquo;s personal EP: 《故乡的风》 (Wind of Home).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)</title><link>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</link><pubDate>Fri, 02 May 2025 16:12:04 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blog.a-moment.top/en/posts/others/arch_on_laptop/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://blog.a-moment.top/images/Alice.png" alt="Featured image of post Installing Arch Linux on a Laptop (Physical Machine)" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Installing Arch Linux on a virtual machine before was just not satisfying enough (lol, you didn&amp;rsquo;t even finish the series (x)), so this time I&amp;rsquo;m putting Arch on my little thin-and-light. And along the way, documenting the pitfalls you might hit on real hardware?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image is from R Sound Design&amp;rsquo;s new track 《アリス？》, a really cheerful Vocaloid song~ Bilibili &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UtV5zqEjC/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;submission&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/aplayer/dist/APlayer.min.css"&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer {&#13;&#10; background: var(--card-background);&#13;&#10; border: 1px solid var(--card-separator-color);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer.aplayer-withlist .aplayer-info {&#13;&#10; border-bottom-color: var(--card-separator-color);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer.aplayer-fixed .aplayer-list {&#13;&#10; border-color: var(--card-separator-color);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-body {&#13;&#10; background-color: var(--card-background);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-info {&#13;&#10; border-top-color: var(--card-background);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-info .aplayer-music .aplayer-title {&#13;&#10; color: var(--card-text-color-main);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-info .aplayer-music .aplayer-author {&#13;&#10; color: var(--card-text-color-secondary);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-info .aplayer-controller .aplayer-time {&#13;&#10; color: var(--card-text-color-tertiary);&#13;&#10;}&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;[data-scheme="dark"] .aplayer .aplayer-info .aplayer-controller .aplayer-time .aplayer-icon path {&#13;&#10; fill: var(--card-text-color-tertiary);&#